IMPORTANT CORRECTIONS — read carefully before planning anything

1. OCR extraction is needed for EXACTLY 3 document types only:
   - screening_adult (Adult Nutrition Screening and Referral Form B.07)
   - screening_pediatric (Pediatric Nutrition Screening and Referral Form B.06)
   - lab_result (Biochemical lab results)
   Inspection reports and marketing statements are PDF OUTPUT only,
   generated from system data. They do NOT need OCR extraction templates.
   The ExtractionTemplateSeeder must only seed 3 templates.

2. The Diagnosis page has 3 domains only: NI, NC, NB.
   There is NO NO (Other) domain. Remove it from all planning.

3. The Intervention Encounter Context tab does NOT have encounter_location.
   The RND always works from their office. Remove encounter_location
   from interventions table and from the tab. Keep only:
   session_type and next_followup_date.

4. Food service inventory is a SEPARATE concern from patient nutrition.
   - food_items table = USDA nutritional database used for patient
     meal planning (nutrient-focused: calories, protein, carbs, fat,
     micronutrients, allergens, unit_price)
   - inventory table = physical stock levels that reference food_items
     (stock-focused: quantity in stock, expiry, usage rate)
   - Food service operations manage physical stock and cost
   - Patient meal plans use food_items for nutritional targeting
   - Both share the food_items table but serve different purposes
   - The food_items content can be seeded with common Philippine
     hospital ingredients to make setup easier when delivered

5. The food service daily budget per patient is 150 pesos.
   budgets.cost_per_person = 150 (pesos, configurable)
   planned_amount is computed as: cost_per_person × active_patient_count
   × days_in_period

6. The Referral tab (Tab E) in Assessment renders the exact visual
   layout of the screening form (adult or pediatric), pre-filled with
   OCR-extracted values. It is not a separate data structure.
   It reads from and writes to screening_documents.extracted_data
   and screening_documents.mapped_fields only.

7. The food service procurement flow has three distinct concepts:
   - Shopping Lists: what ingredients need to be purchased
     (can be manually created or auto-suggested from menu vs stock)
   - Purchase Orders: formal POs created from shopping lists,
     sent to a specific supplier, with status tracking
   - Suppliers: supplier directory with contact and payment terms

