IMPORTANT: OCR extraction is for 3 document types ONLY.
Inspection reports and marketing statements are PDF OUTPUT only.

Plan OCRService:
  Location: app/Services/OCRService.php
  Single public method: extract(string $filePath): string
  HTTP POST to PADDLEOCR_URL env var (default: http://paddleocr:5000/ocr)
  Timeout: 30 seconds
  Retries: 3 with exponential backoff
  Returns: raw extracted text string
  On failure: throws exception, logs to Laravel log
  Mock implementation: return sample text based on document_type
    for development until M4 live testing
  Called only from Jobs, never directly from controllers

Plan ExtractionService:
  Location: app/Services/ExtractionService.php
  Main method: parse(string $rawText, string $documentType): ParsedDocument
  Loads matching extraction_template from database by document_type
  Applies field_mappings using regex and checkbox detection patterns
  Scores confidence per field: 0.0 to 1.0
    - Exact pattern match = 1.0
    - Partial match = 0.5 to 0.8
    - Value within expected range adds +0.2
  Returns ParsedDocument DTO
  Logs everything to extraction_logs table

Plan ParsedDocument DTO:
  Location: app/DTOs/ParsedDocument.php
  Properties:
    fields: array (extracted key-value pairs)
    confidenceScores: array (per-field float 0.0-1.0)
    rawText: string
    documentType: string
    processingTimeMs: int
    errors: array

Plan ProcessDocumentExtraction Job:
  Location: app/Jobs/ProcessDocumentExtraction.php
  Accepts: document_id, document_type, target_model, target_id
  Flow:
    1. Call OCRService::extract(filePath) → raw text
    2. Call ExtractionService::parse(rawText, documentType) → ParsedDocument
    3. Store parsed_fields and confidence_scores on source record
    4. Update source record status to completed
    5. Fire DocumentExtractionCompleted event
  Runs on Redis queue
  On failure: update status to failed, log error

Plan DocumentExtractionCompleted Event:
  Location: app/Events/DocumentExtractionCompleted.php
  Carries: document_id, document_type, target_model, target_id, confidence_score

