PART 3 — RISK SCORE CALCULATION

The risk score is calculated from the 7 checkboxes exactly as shown
on the NCP form (Medical Nutrition Therapy / Nutrition Care Plan form
from the hospital reference documents).

Risk scoring factors and point values:
  1. Screening criteria for potential nutritional risk = 1 point
  2. Less than 85% or greater than 130% ideal body weight = 1 point
  3. Unintentional weight loss ___% over ___ weeks/months = 2 points
     Also capture from this item:
       assessments.weight_loss_percentage (decimal)
       assessments.weight_loss_period (string)
  4. Mechanical / digestive problem = 1 point
  5. Low albumin = 1 point
  6. Significant lab result = 1 point
  7. Other/s = 1 point

Score thresholds:
  Total = 1 → Low Risk → Nutritional Status: Normal
  Total = 2 or 3 → Moderate → Nutritional Status: Moderate Malnutrition
  Total > 3 → High Risk → Nutritional Status: Severe Malnutrition

Where calculation runs:
  - After ProcessDocumentExtraction Job completes for a screening document
  - When RND manually saves the Referral/Screening tab

Where results are stored:
  ncp_records.risk_score = numeric total (decimal)
  assessments.nutritional_status = derived label enum

Where the risk score UI section appears:
  On the Assessment page, the risk score section renders AFTER Tab E
  (Referral/Screening form) and BEFORE Tab F (RND Summary).
  This matches the position on the physical NCP form where the
  "Scoring of Nutritional Risk Related Factors" section appears
  after the assessment data and before the nutrition diagnosis.

Risk score UI display:
  Show each of the 7 checkboxes with their point values
  Show which are checked (from OCR or manual input)
  Show running total
  Show risk level badge: Low (green), Moderate (amber), High (red)
  Show nutritional status label
  RND can manually check/uncheck and recalculate

