Food Restrictions and Recommendations Panel:
  IMPORTANT: This panel is 100% algorithm-driven. There is NO AI here.
  Powered by RecommendService reading from clinical_rules table.
  
  Data sources read by RecommendService (in order of priority):
    assessments.allergies (json) → HARD FILTER: never include these foods
    assessments.food_dislikes (json) → SOFT: shown as warning note to RND only,
      never hard-excluded from meal plan or recommendations
    patients.religion + assessments.lifestyle → HARD FILTER:
      religious/cultural restrictions (e.g. no pork for Muslim patients,
      no beef for Hindu patients)
    assessments.medications (json) → food-drug interaction check
      against hardcoded interaction rules
    diagnoses.domain + diagnoses.problem → identify patient conditions
    interventions.goal_type + interventions.disease_stage → apply
      clinical rules from clinical_rules table
    biochemical_data → lab value refinement:
      high potassium → stricter potassium restriction even without CKD
      low albumin → prioritize high protein foods
      high glucose → stricter carbohydrate restriction
    food_items.allergens + food_items.micronutrients → match against filters

  Display output:
    RECOMMEND list: foods/nutrients to include, with reason per item
    AVOID list: foods/nutrients to exclude, with reason per item

Current Meal Plan Summary (real-time tracker):
  Shows current vs target for each displayed nutrient:
    Energy: current kcal / target kcal
    Protein: current g / target g
    Carbs: current g / target g
    Fat: current g / target g
  Color coded: green if within 10% of target, red if >10% off

Weekly Meal Plan (7 days × 5 meal types):
  Days: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday
  Meal types: Breakfast, AM Snack, Lunch, PM Snack, Dinner
  Each cell: add food items or full recipes
  Food items auto-calculate nutrients from food_items table
  Recipes auto-calculate nutrients from recipe totals
  Nutrient snapshot frozen at time of planning
    (stored as meal_plan_items.nutrient_snapshot json)
  Load template from meal_plan_templates table
  Save current plan as new template to meal_plan_templates table
  AI-suggested items labeled "AI Suggested — Pending RND Review"
    (meal_plan_items.ai_suggested = true)
  Patient food dislikes shown as warning note in meal plan cells
    but NOT filtered out — RND decides

Meal Plan Auto-Generation Algorithm (MealPlanService):
  GATE: Requires minimum 15 recipes in recipes table.
    If below threshold: show prompt to RND, do not auto-generate.
  
  Step 1: Read from assessment
    allergies → hard exclude (never include these food items or recipes
      containing these allergens)
    religious/cultural restrictions from patients.religion → hard exclude
  
  Step 2: Read nutrition prescription from interventions
    energy_kcal, protein_g, carbs_g, fat_g, fluid_ml, micronutrient_limits
  
  Step 3: Query recipe library
    Filter out recipes that contain allergens or restricted ingredients
    Score each recipe by nutrient fit to prescription targets
    (closer to proportional target = higher score)
  
  Step 4: Query food_items for snacks
    Same allergen and restriction filters applied
    Score by nutrient fit
  
  Step 5: Build 7-day plan
    Assign highest-scoring recipes to main meals
    Assign best-fit food items to snack slots
    Ensure variety (no recipe repeated more than twice per week)
    Adjust quantities mathematically to hit daily targets
  
  Step 6: Validate each day
    Sum all nutrients for the day
    Within 10% of targets → flag meal_plan_days.flagged = false (green)
    More than 10% off any target → flag meal_plan_days.flagged = true
      (requires RND review)
  
  Step 7: AI fallback (claude-sonnet-4-6) ONLY if fewer than 5 recipes
    pass the filter after allergen/restriction exclusion
    Label these: "AI Suggested — Pending RND Review"
    Set meal_plan_items.ai_suggested = true
    This is the ONLY case where AI is used in meal planning

