The food service module manages physical ingredient stock,
weekly meal planning for the hospital kitchen, budget tracking,
and procurement. It is separate from patient NCP meal planning.

IMPORTANT DISTINCTION:
  Patient meal plans (NCP Intervention) = nutrient-focused,
    uses food_items USDA nutritional data, targets macros/micros
  Food service operations = stock-focused and cost-focused,
    uses food_items for physical inventory, targets 150 peso/day/patient

7A — INVENTORY PAGE

Purpose: Manage physical ingredient stock levels, track expiry,
  monitor restock needs.

Data columns displayed (from inventory table joined with food_items):
  Ingredient Name (food_items.name)
  Category (food_items.category — Protein, Carbohydrate, Dairy, Fats,
    Vegetables, Fruits, Condiments, etc.)
  Quantity in Stock (inventory.quantity_in_stock)
  Unit (inventory.unit — kg, piece, liter, bundle, pack, etc.)
  Unit Price (food_items.unit_price — for cost computation)
  Expiry Date (inventory.expiry_date)
  Usage Rate (inventory.usage_rate — optional notes on consumption)
  Minimum Stock Threshold (inventory.minimum_stock_threshold)
  Alert Status (computed):
    LOW STOCK: quantity_in_stock <= minimum_stock_threshold
    EXPIRING SOON: expiry_date within 3 days of today
    EXPIRED: expiry_date is in the past

Quick Dashboard Cards:
  Total Ingredients (count of inventory rows)
  Low Stock Alerts (count where quantity <= threshold)
  Expiring Soon (count within 3 days)
  Top Used Ingredients (based on usage_rate field)

Actions per row:
  Restock (updates quantity_in_stock)
  Edit (updates any inventory field)
  Remove (soft delete or mark inactive)
  View History (audit trail from spatie activity log)

All edits are logged via AuditMiddleware for audit trail.

7B — MENU CYCLE PAGE (Weekly Planner)

Purpose: Plan weekly hospital meals with cost awareness.
Data: menu_cycles + menu_cycle_days tables

Layout: 7-day × 5 meal type grid (same structure as patient meal plan
  but for hospital kitchen, not individual patient)

Features:
  Plan meals for Monday through Sunday
  Each cell: select recipe or individual food item
  Meal types: Breakfast, AM Snack, Lunch, PM Snack, Dinner
  Daily cost per person computed automatically:
    Sum of (food_items.unit_price × quantity used) for all
    items in that day's meals, divided by estimated patient count
  Budget awareness display:
    Green = daily cost per person <= 150 pesos
    Yellow = daily cost per person between 140 and 150 pesos
    Red = daily cost per person > 150 pesos
  Save as template for reuse
  Load previously saved menu cycle as starting template
  Activate a menu cycle: sets status to active, sets activation_date
    FSS role can view activated menu cycles as read-only

